---
import WorksheetLayout from '../../../../layouts/WorksheetLayout.astro';
---
<WorksheetLayout
  title="SIFT Fact Check"
  lesson="/courses/mfedu-2026/true-enough-to-wear/"
  intro="Before a claim goes on your runway piece, run it through SIFT. One sheet per claim."
>
  <h2>The claim I want to put on my piece</h2>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>
  <p class="ws-hint">Example: "The fashion industry is the 2nd largest polluter in the world."</p>

  <h2>🛑 Stop</h2>
  <p>Where did I first hear this? How sure am I that it's true, from 1 (a guess) to 5 (certain)?</p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>

  <h2>🔍 Investigate the source</h2>
  <p>Who is telling me this, and what do <em>other people</em> say about that source?</p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>

  <h2>🔎 Find better coverage</h2>
  <p>What do at least two other trustworthy sources say about the same claim?</p>
  <p><strong>Source 1:</strong></p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>
  <p><strong>Source 2:</strong></p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>

  <h2>🔗 Trace it back</h2>
  <p>Where did the claim originally come from (study, speech, photo, statistic)? Does the original say what everyone claims it says?</p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>

  <h2>Verdict</h2>
  <ul class="ws-checks">
    <li>Solid — I can put this on my piece as-is</li>
    <li>Partly true — I'll adjust the wording to what I can back up</li>
    <li>Busted — I'm dropping it (and I know something true to say instead)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>What my piece will actually say:</p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>
</WorksheetLayout>
